    <section class="empire-glance" id="at-a-glance" aria-labelledby="glance-title">
      <div class="empire-glance-main"><h2 class="empire-glance-title" id="glance-title">At a glance</h2><ul><li>After the Jurchen-led Jin dynasty took <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/north-china">North China</a> in the Jingkang Incident, the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/song-dynasty">Song</a> court retreated south of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/yangtze-river">Yangtze</a> and established its capital at Lin'an.</li><li>The <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/song-dynasty">Song dynasty</a> established <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/china">China</a>'s first permanent navy in 1132, with a headquarters at Dinghai.</li><li><a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kublai-khan">Kublai Khan</a>'s armies conquered the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/song-dynasty">Southern Song</a> in 1279 after the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/battle-of-yamen">Battle of Yamen</a>, reuniting <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/china">China</a> under the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/yuan-dynasty">Yuan dynasty</a>.</li></ul></div>
      <aside class="empire-dyk"><p class="empire-dyk-title">Did you know?</p><p>In 1161, at the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/battle-of-caishi">Battle of Caishi</a> and the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/battle-of-tangdao">Battle of Tangdao</a>, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/song-dynasty">Song</a> forces of 3,000 men on 120 warships defeated a Jin fleet said to number 70,000 men on 600 warships, using paddle wheel-driven vessels and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/gunpowder">gunpowder</a> bombs.</p></aside>
    </section>

